विक्रमः ।",
      "textEn": "21\n\nOf him—of that (Bhoomaasura); Atma-jah—son; Ayam—this; Tava—yours; Pada—feet; Pankajam—like a lotus; Bhita—\nfrightened; Prapanna— seeking refuge; Aarti—sorrow, grief; Hara— O destroyer; Upasaditah— has come; Tat—therefore; Palay—\nprotect; Enam—his; Kuru— keep; Hasta-pankajam—your lotus-like hand; Shirasi— on the head; Amushya— his; Akhil—\nall; Kalmasha— sin; Apaham— completely destroying. This is the son of Bhaumasura. This is frightened and is coming near your lotus feet.\nBecause you take away the sufferings of all those who come to your refuge. Please protect it.\nPlease protect it. You should place your lotus-like hand upon its head, which is the remover of all sins. Meaning: This Mother Earth is asking for protection for her grandson, who is very scared by the recent terrible\nevents. Srisuka said:\nThus, the Lord, pleased with the earth, spoke with the devotees.\nHaving come to the earth, fearless, and having entered the house. 2. Meaning of the word.\n\nShri-Shuka said—Shukadeva Goswami said; Thus—in this way; Bhumi—by the goddess of earth; Arthitah—upon being prayed;\nVagbhih—by those words; Bhagavan—God; Bhakti—devoutly; Namraya—with humility; Dattvam—giving; Abhayam—fearless; Bhaum-\nGriham—in the house of Bhaumasura; Pravishat—entered; Sakal—all; Riddhi—with wealth; Mat—joined..\n\nShukdev Goswami said: Thus, upon the request made by the goddess of the earth with humble devotion,\nupon departing, God granted his grandson refuge, and then entered the palace of Bhaumasura,\nwhich was full of all kinds of opulence. There, the king's daughters, six thousand and more years old. Hari was seen by the earth-born, victorious kings. Meaning of the word\n\nTatra—there; Rajanya—of the royal class; Kanyanaam—of the maidens; Shat-Sahastra—six thousand; Adhik—more than; Ayutam—ten; Bhouma—by Bhouma; Ahrutanam—seized; Vikramya—by force; Rajabhyah—from the kings; Dadrisha—seen; Harih—Lord\nKrishna.\nThere, Lord Krishna saw more than sixteen thousand princesses, whom Bhaum had forcefully taken away from various kings. Meaning: Srila Sridhar Swami presents that evidence of Parashara Muni, as it is quoted in Vishnu Purana\n(5.29.1), according to which, 16 0 princesses were imprisoned in the palace of Bhaum:\n\nKanyapure sa kanyanam shodashatulyavikramah."
