      "textEn": "24\n\nEstablished: — Established; Satyabhama: — Satyabhama's; Home: — Of the house; Garden: — Of the garden; Adornment: — While making beautiful;\nFollower: — Behind; Bumblebees: — Bumblebees; From heaven: — From heaven; That: His; Fragrance: — Fragrance; Intoxicant: — And of sweet juice;\nCovetous: — Greedy..\n\nOnce planted, the Parijat tree made the garden of Queen Satyabhama's palace beautiful. The bees, greedy for the fragrance and sweet juice of this tree,\nwere chasing it from heaven itself. Yayaacha aanamya kiritakotibhih\nPadau spruhannaachyutamarthasadhanam.\nSiddhartha is not separated from the great\nNot from the darkness of the gods. 41. Meaning of the word:\n\nYayach—He (Indra) made a request; Aanamya—bowing down; Kirit—of the crown; Kotibhih—with noses; Padau—their feet;\nSprushan—touching; Achyutam—to Lord Krishna; Artha—his (Indra's) work; Sadhanam—to complete;\nSiddha—completed; Arthah—whose purpose; Eten—with them; Vigrihyate—quarrels; Mahan—great; Aho—indeed;\nSuranam—of the gods; Cha—and; Tamah—darkness; Dhikh—condemnation; Aadhityam—their wealth..\n\nTo salute Lord Achyuta, to touch his feet with the tips of his crown,\nand even after pleading to God to fulfill his wish, that great deity\nafter getting his work done, wanted to quarrel with God. What ignorance is this, O Gods! Shame on their glory. Meaning: It is well known that immoderation comes from material possessions and rights, therefore, often\na luxurious life becomes the path that paves the way to hell.\nThen, at the auspicious time, the women. In the proper measure, the Lord is the form of the unchanging. 42. Meaning of the word\n\nAtha u—and then; Muhurte—at an auspicious time; Ekasmin—in that; Nana—many; Agareshu—in the buildings; Taha—they; Striyah—women;\nYatha—in a proper manner; Upayame—married; Bhagavan—God; Tavat—that much; Rupa—form; Dharah—while assuming;\nAvyayah—indestructible. Then, that immensely powerful man, taking separate forms for each bride,\nmarried all the princesses together in their respective palaces. Meaning: As explained by Srila Sridhar Goswami, here the word 'yatha' indicates that"
