      "textEn": "7\n\nAccording to the self, worship the Kshatriya king. Yena tvamashishah satya ihamutra cha lapsyase. 17. Meaning of the word\n\nAth—Now; Atmanah—your own; Samanuraktam—suitable; Vai—indeed; Bhajasva—accept; Kshatriya-rishabham—to a high-class royal family; Yena—by which; Tvam—you; Ashishah—hopes; Satyah—that which can be fulfilled; Iha—in this life;\nAmurtham—in the next life; Cha—also; Lapsyase—you will attain. Now you need to accept a more suitable, of higher order, noble man,\nTake him who can help you in attaining every such thing in this life and also in the next life,\nWhich you desire. Meaning: Lord Krishna is going to tease his beautiful wife by awakening her sensual mood. Chaityashalavajarasandha dantavakradayo nripaah.\nMam dvishanti vamoru rukmi chaapi tavagraja. 18. Meaning of the words.\n\nChaitya-Shalva-Jarasandha-Dantavakra-Adayaha -Chaitya (Shishupala), Shalva, Jarasandha, Dantavakra, etc.; Nripaaha -Rajaagana; Mama -Mine; Dvishanti -They hate; Vaama-Uru -Hey, with beautiful thighs; Rukmi -Rukmi; Cha Api -Also; Tava -Yours; Agra-Jah -\nElder brother..\n\nThese beautiful, lady-like, Bhadre, Shishupal, Shalva, Jarasandha, and Dantavakra, all kings hate me.\nAnd in the same way, your elder brother Rukmi also does. Of them, to the best of the brave, to the steadfast, to the wise. Anitasi Maya Bhadre Tejopaharatasataam. 19. Meaning of the word\n\nTesham—Of all; Virya—Of one's own power; Mad—Intoxicated; Andhaham—Being blind; Druttanam—Arrogant; Smaya—Arrogance;\nNuttaye—To remove; Aanita Asi—You were taken away in marriage; Maya—By me; Bhadre—Auspicious, auspicious woman;\nTejah—Strength; Upaharta—Removing; Astatam—Of the wicked.\n.\n\nIt is to remove the arrogance of these kings that I have brought you here, O Kalyani.\nBecause they were all blinded by the intoxication of power. My purpose was to crush the power of the evil ones. In sorrow, we are not for the sake of pleasing others. Self-realization is the complete house, the action o